// This is the actual "Writing Function" body pasted into the Deals custom button itself
// (Setup > Deals > Buttons > New Custom Button > "Retry CRM Sync" > Action Type = Writing
// Function). A button's inline body gets an implicit `deal` variable but is NOT itself
// where the retry logic lives -- it just calls the real named Custom Function
// (retryPreNeedCrmSync.deluge, created separately under Setup > Automation > Functions)
// and shows the result.
//
// Called with the standalone. prefix -- this org's established convention for cross-calling
// a standalone Custom Function (see [[feedback_deluge_automation_vs_standalone_calls]]: the
// prefix matters here, it's only *automation*-category functions that need a REST call
// instead). If Setup rejects this call shape, the function may need re-creating under a
// different category -- check that before assuming the retry logic itself is wrong.
response = standalone.retryPreNeedCrmSync(deal.id);
respMap = response.toMap();
alert ifnull(respMap.get("message"),"Retry finished.");
